        "detailed_description": "<h1>WHAT'S THE DIFFERENCE?</h1><p><p class=\"bb_paragraph\" ><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/c3e4f52240bce1545052298c98803777.avif?t=1786716632\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras_big/c3e4f52240bce1545052298c98803777.avif?t=1786716632 width=1560 height=1970 /></span></p></p><br><h1>JOIN OUR DISCORD</h1><p><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><img class=\"bb_img\" src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/81310aa138c0daa7aced90b5a6e7e6ac.avif?t=1786716632\" data-big-src=https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras_big/81310aa138c0daa7aced90b5a6e7e6ac.avif?t=1786716632 width=800 height=208 /></span></p><br><h1>About the Game</h1>Before <strong>Eufloria HD (2014)</strong>, there was <strong>Eufloria (2009)</strong>. The long-unlisted indie classic is available once again for the 15 year anniversary. Updated to run on modern systems, with new content, features, and expanded moddability.<br><br>Old school intergalactic floral warfare is BACK! (Warts and all!)<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/dbe5d8650ccdd83ae8c7b831e818122d.poster.avif?t=1786716632\" width=1170 height=274 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/dbe5d8650ccdd83ae8c7b831e818122d.webm?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/dbe5d8650ccdd83ae8c7b831e818122d.mp4?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Before You Buy</strong></h2><br><strong>Eufloria Classic</strong> is a re-release of the original version of <strong>Eufloria (2009)</strong>, with some modern quality of life changes, and not a new Eufloria game nor a sequel to <strong>Eufloria HD (2014)</strong>. It is a “warts and all” anniversary release, with only non-disruptive changes or objective improvements made. Anything that affects the “feel” of the <strong>original Eufloria</strong> has remained unchanged.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Is this for me?</strong></h2>While <strong>Eufloria HD</strong> boasts a number of improvements lacking in <strong>Eufloria Classic</strong>, we are offering a number of things not available elsewhere:<br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>It is the only release that supports mods and custom levels, and is backward compatible with all previously released mods that work with the original game.<br></li><li>We included two entirely new game modes, with two sample levels per mode. We plan to release more together with the modding community.<br></li><li>Entirely new music from the original composer for the game, Milieu.<br></li><li>Finally; for some people the original version is the preferred version, despite its limitations, and this allows them to play it once again, pretty much exactly how they remembered it.</li></ul><br><strong>Eufloria Classic</strong> is free to all owners of <strong>Eufloria (2009)</strong>, simply update and launch that version in your Steam library to see a new option to play <strong>Eufloria Classic</strong>. It is also heavily discounted for owners of <strong>Eufloria HD (2014)</strong> via the Steam bundle linked above.<br><br><strong>Eufloria (2009)</strong> is from a bygone age of small monitors, and as such does not always play nicely with high resolution displays (1440p/4K). The game will still run at high resolutions, but your mileage may vary on visual scaling. If you have a 1440p or higher display, we recommend downloading the demo first to make sure the game displays correctly for you.<br><br>If you do encounter issues, there might still be workarounds. These are listed and kept up to date on our Steam forums.<h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Grow your own Units</strong></h2><br>Conquer asteroids in space and use their resources to grow <strong>floral creatures</strong> that do the player's bidding. <strong>Expand your empire</strong> and fight for resources against several teams of opponents that all vie for the same resources and can offer fierce opposition.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/0ce959360e0c73c2ed82627dbb59ee55.poster.avif?t=1786716632\" width=1170 height=274 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/0ce959360e0c73c2ed82627dbb59ee55.webm?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/0ce959360e0c73c2ed82627dbb59ee55.mp4?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Timeless, Gorgeous and Accessible</strong></h2><br>Presented in a unique and gorgeous <strong>floral aesthetic</strong>, the game can be played competitively or in a relaxed, ambient style. <i>You</i> choose how to play.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/d87bc3be007778451e3ed7ab72089ae8.poster.avif?t=1786716632\" width=1170 height=274 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/d87bc3be007778451e3ed7ab72089ae8.webm?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/d87bc3be007778451e3ed7ab72089ae8.mp4?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Endless Replayability</strong></h2><br>Along a <strong>25 level campaign mode</strong>, a host of additional modes offer <strong>procedural levels</strong> that offer endless replayability. Add to that a vast number of <strong>mods and user levels</strong> plus an active mod community and you will not soon run out of challenges.<br><br><span class=\"bb_img_ctn\"><video class=\"bb_img\" autoplay muted loop playsinline poster=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/98bf1d1d89681645ac432aec1767e6d6.poster.avif?t=1786716632\" width=1170 height=274 ><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/98bf1d1d89681645ac432aec1767e6d6.webm?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/webm; codecs=vp9\"><source src=\"https://shared.akamai.steamstatic.com/store_item_assets/steam/apps/3254570/extras/98bf1d1d89681645ac432aec1767e6d6.mp4?t=1786716632\" type=\"video/mp4\"></video></span><h2 class=\"bb_tag\" ><strong>Features:</strong></h2><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>25 level Single player campaign<br></li><li>8 Level “Skirmish Mode”<br></li><li>Unlockable “Dark Matter” mode<br></li><li>Hours of wonderful ambient music by “Milieu”<br></li><li>Procedural levels – great for replayability<br></li><li>Community levels<br></li><li>And more</li></ul>But to <strong>celebrate</strong> the new release and reward loyal fans we have also added:<br><ul class=\"bb_ul\"><li>New “Regrowth” Game Mode<br></li><li>New &quot;Gardening&quot; Mode<br></li><li>New original music by “Milieu&quot;<br></li><li>Enhanced modding options<br></li><li>Game Speedup buttons<br></li><li>A whole treasure trove of bonus files, art, stories, and concepts<br></li><li>Updated UI support<br></li><li>Updated Demo</li></ul>",
